      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm having some trouble with an iam policy. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to a specific s3 bucket but i keep getting an access denied error. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u take a look at this json and see what i'm missing?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The IAM policy you've provided allows the `s3:PutObject` action for the specified S3 bucket, but it doesn't explicitly allow your Lambda function to write logs. To grant Lambda permission, you need to use the `aws:SourceArn` context, which identifies the source of the request. Add the `aws:SourceArn` context along with a \"Resources\" statement for your Lambda function. For example:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:PutObjectAcl\",\n        \"logs:CreateLogGroup\",\n        \"logs:CreateLogStream\",\n        \"logs:PutLogEvents\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": [\n        \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket/*\",\n        \"*\",\n        \"arn:aws:logs:*:*:*\"\n      ],\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringLike\": {\n          \"aws:SourceArn\": [\"arn:aws:lambda:*:*:function:<your-lambda-functions-name>\"]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThis",
      "source": "target",
